 "text": "Your next customer might be an AI with a spending limit. Walmart just let AI shopping assistants buy in its store. They get a budget, they ask for approval, and they can be switched off. These assistants don't scroll your photos. They read. Four things first. Sizes and materials. Real stock. A delivery date. And returns in plain words. If one is missing, they move on to the next store. ContentSystems.ai helps online brands keep all four complete and right. Want our agent ready checklist? Comment systems and we'll send it to you free."
